Title: AROS clipboard backend for the clip library
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: On AROS the clip library used clip_none.cpp: copy and paste worked only inside LibreSprite; nothing reached or came from other programs (text or pictures).
Change: clip/clip_aros.cpp on clipboard.device unit 0 with iffparse: text as FTXT (CHRS in the system character set plus a UTF8 chunk; reading prefers UTF8), pictures written as 24-bit ILBM like AROS Capture (what ilbm.datatype reads) and read through the datatypes (DTST_CLIPBOARD, PDTM_READPIXELARRAY RGBA, opaque unless the picture has an alpha mask), custom formats kept in the process and dropped when the clip ID changes. clip links base-lib, datatypes and iffparse on AROS.
Scope: AROS
Upstream: local-only (AROS backend; could be offered to the clip library later)
Verification: mainline x86_64, pool v1-1, 2026-11-16: AROS Capture picture pasted (size taken for New Sprite), LibreSprite picture shown by MultiView CLIPBOARD, text to the Shell, Latin-2 FTXT pasted as UTF-8, own copy replaced by a newer Capture clip, own copy and paste inside LibreSprite; evidence docs/evidence/2026-11-16-clipboard-v1
Removal: AROS-specific.
---
